// @run
// @log 0
// @hint Intentionally-unused parameter `_x` (leading `_` marks it unused)
// THE GATE THIS FILE PINNED IS GONE, AND THIS FILE IS WHY IT COULD GO. Kept — unchanged
// below the header — as the ROUTE pin it always was: an array-of-declared-struct alias
// standing as a UNION ARM in a parameter compiles and runs. What is retired is the reason.
//
// It read: "`singleMemberAliasName` hands the emitter `tyToEmitName(m)`, and that renders a
// declared struct element STRUCTURALLY — `Cat[]` becomes `{n:i32}[]` — dropping the nominal
// name the emitter's element tables key on. That IS the 'nominal emit route to lose' #1137
// warned about … So the transparency arm is gated on `arrSpineIsScalar` … Widening the arm
// to every `TyArray` turns this file red — which is the sabotage that says the gate is
// load-bearing rather than lazily narrow."
//
// Every clause of that is true of the RENDERER and none of it is true of the widening. The
// arm now admits a DECLARED-STRUCT leaf too (`arrSpineIsNominal`) and renders it with
// `tyToNominalName`, the name-faithful twin that was already written and had no consumer in
// emitted output at all — so the member spells `Cat[]`, which is character for character the
// DIRECT annotation, and the route below is kept rather than lost. **The predicted sabotage
// does not fire: this file is green under the widening**, measured, which is the one thing
// the old header asserted that turned out to be about `tyToEmitName` rather than about
// `TyArray`.
//
// The gate's price is in `array-alias-nominal-element.vl` (the plain-struct element was the
// loud `struct array elements are not supported`, the union-ARM element was check-clean
// invalid wasm — silent-class-inventory D49, and every reading use was a checker reject that
// read as nonsense). This file stays as the other direction's witness: substituting the
// STRUCTURAL render for `L` still turns it into
// ``emitProgram: only i32, i64, f64, f32, boolean, struct, union, array, or string
// parameters are supported``, so the nominal renderer is load-bearing even though the gate
// was not.
type Cat = { n: i32 }
type L = Cat[]

function tag(_x: L | i32) {
  return 0
}

print(tag(1))
